{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Data Consistency & Validation Rules\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements systematic validation rules to catch corrupt records before analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Validation Categories Implemented:\n",
    "1. **Range Checks**: Age (0-150), Price ($\ge 0$), Birth Date (1920 to Today)\n",
    "2. **Null Constraints**: `customer_id` and `email` not missing\n",
    "3. **Format Pattern Validation**: Email `@` structure and 10-digit phone regex\n",
    "4. **Business Rule Validation**: Campaign `end_date` $\ge$ `start_date`\n",
    "5. **Validation Report & Failure Isolation**: Summary counts, failure isolation to `output/validation_failures.csv`, clean data export"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load raw dataset\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/customer_validation_data.csv')\n",
    "df.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 1: Range Checks\n",
    "\n",
    "Validate age between 0 and 150, non-negative prices, and realistic birth dates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['valid_age'] = (df['age'] >= 0) & (df['age'] <= 150)\n",
    "df['valid_price'] = df['price'] >= 0\n",
    "birth_dt = pd.to_datetime(df['birth_date'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "df['valid_date'] = (birth_dt >= pd.Timestamp('1920-01-01')) & (birth_dt <= pd.Timestamp.now())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid ages: {(~df['valid_age']).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid prices: {(~df['valid_price']).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid birth dates: {(~df['valid_date']).sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 2: Null Constraints\n",
    "\n",
    "Ensure critical primary keys and identity fields (`customer_id`, `email`) are never null."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['valid_customer_id'] = df['customer_id'].notna()\n",
    "df['valid_email'] = df['email'].notna()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Missing customer IDs: {(~df['valid_customer_id']).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Missing emails: {(~df['valid_email']).sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 3: Format Pattern Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "Validate email structures and phone number digit patterns using regex."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['valid_email_format'] = df['email'].astype(str).str.contains('@', na=False) & df['email'].notna()\n",
    "df['valid_phone'] = df['phone'].astype(str).str.match(r'^\\d{10}$', na=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid emails: {(~df['valid_email_format']).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid phones: {(~df['valid_phone']).sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 4: Business Rule Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "Ensure campaign `end_date` is on or after `start_date`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "start_dt = pd.to_datetime(df['start_date'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "end_dt = pd.to_datetime(df['end_date'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "df['valid_date_order'] = (end_dt >= start_dt) & start_dt.notna() & end_dt.notna()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid date ranges: {(~df['valid_date_order']).sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 5: Validation Report & Failure Isolation\n",
    "\n",
    "Combine all validation checks, isolate bad records into `output/validation_failures.csv`, and produce clean analytical dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "validation_cols = [\n",
    "    'valid_age', 'valid_price', 'valid_date', \n",
    "    'valid_customer_id', 'valid_email_format', 'valid_date_order'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df['passes_all_checks'] = df[validation_cols].all(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Isolate failures\n",
    "failures = df[~df['passes_all_checks']]\n",
    "os.makedirs('../output', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "failures.to_csv('../output/validation_failures.csv', index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Report\n",
    "print(f\"Records: {len(df)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Passed: {df['passes_all_checks'].sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Failed: {(~df['passes_all_checks']).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean = df[df['passes_all_checks']]\n",
    "os.makedirs('../data/processed', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "df_clean.to_csv('../data/processed/validated_customer_data.csv', index=False)"
   ]
  }
 ],
